WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:10.940
Hey, welcome back to 40 Days of Holiness. Grab your workbook.

2
00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:14.920
Let's get started. Today's theme is about the sin

3
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.940
nature one more time, all right? And so it's a challenging one.

4
00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:22.460
Here it is. This is day 12. We're going to talk about how the

5
00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:25.060
twistedness inside disguises itself.

6
00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:28.280
I imagine you remember probably playing hide and seek when you were a kid.

7
00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:31.720
You remember that one place that you ever found to hide, that place that

8
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:35.500
nobody could see, nobody could ever find you right there, right?

9
00:00:35.990 --> 00:00:38.880
The sinful nature is really good at hide and seek.

10
00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:43.140
If you've ever seen someone do sleight of hand, right, that was really good at it,

11
00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:45.760
they do the old cups and balls trick.

12
00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:48.760
They say, "I'm going to take this one right here. We're going to take it.

13
00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:51.980
We're going to take it like this, and we're going to take it and vanish it," and

14
00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:54.460
then it appears back under the cup. Whoops.

15
00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:58.120
And then it appears back under the cup, and you say, "Well, here's another one

16
00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:00.100
right here. I know, let's get rid of that one.

17
00:01:00.290 --> 00:01:01.780
Surely we can do this one." You take it.

18
00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:04.990
I love doing it for kids because they're always so surprised when you take it and

19
00:01:05.041 --> 00:01:05.560
you vanish it.

20
00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:10.060
And then you take it and appears back under the cup, and you say, "Well, that's

21
00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:13.420
it. I'm going to take it right here." And you reach out and you grab one in midair,

22
00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:17.130
and you take it like this and say, "All right, let's take it and get rid..." And

23
00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:19.590
there it is right there. And we're going to take it, drove it right through, down

24
00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:21.900
into the... And we're going to take it like this right here.

25
00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:25.830
And then when you think you've got them all, there's more, and they just keep

26
00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:28.560
appearing. I know, that's just a silly illustration.

27
00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:30.700
I like playing around with it. But here's the thing.

28
00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:33.280
Sinful nature can feel very much

29
00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:36.840
like someone is doing sleight of sin with you.

30
00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:42.200
Now, let's get rid of all that. Let's go to the scripture.

31
00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:46.040
Today my goal is to help you pull back the camouflage, see

32
00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:48.820
behind it, and catch what's really going on.

33
00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:52.790
Jeremiah 17:9 says this: "The heart is deceitful

34
00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:56.480
above all things and beyond cure." Or King James will say,

35
00:01:56.600 --> 00:02:00.550
"Desperately wicked." "Who can understand it?" Now,

36
00:02:00.570 --> 00:02:03.820
I'm going to come back to that beyond cure later, and we'll talk about what God can

37
00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:05.550
do to cure the incurable. All right?

38
00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:09.980
But I want you to not miss that last phrase, "Who can understand it?"

39
00:02:10.861 --> 00:02:14.100
The implication is that we can't even understand it.

40
00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:17.370
The sinful nature is a master of disguise, and it

41
00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:20.220
remains in the human heart after salvation.

42
00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:23.200
Now, salvation is powerful, wonderful, and great.

43
00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:26.720
New creation, old things pass away, all things are new.

44
00:02:26.780 --> 00:02:29.220
It's amazing to be saved and a new creation.

45
00:02:29.780 --> 00:02:33.000
What it means is that you completely start over. Your guilt is gone.

46
00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:36.700
Your conscience is cleansed. It's as if everything in the world is

47
00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:40.000
done and finished, and you're raised from death to life.

48
00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:42.460
You're adopted into God's family. It's wonderful.

49
00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:47.380
But every theological system from every denomination recognizes this is

50
00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:51.060
the case. That the cowboy in me, the nature of sin remains.

51
00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:54.720
Catholics believe it, Presbyterians believe it, Methodists, Baptists,

52
00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:55.580
Pentecostals,

53
00:02:56.780 --> 00:03:00.600
and more. They all believe that. Now, that's hard to get five different

54
00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:03.829
denominations in a room and have them agree on anything,

55
00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:07.600
right? But they all recognize this one as true.

56
00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:09.960
We have actions of sin,

57
00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:14.720
but behind them is the nature of sin itself, and that nature remains

58
00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:18.630
in the heart after the actions of sin are forgiven and

59
00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:21.760
we're regenerated in the new birth. It is bound, yes.

60
00:03:21.820 --> 00:03:25.730
It is weakened, yes. It is not ruling, but the sin nature is

61
00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:28.260
present. So what is the sin nature?

62
00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:31.700
Well, it is a warping of the human spirit

63
00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:34.120
caused by the absence

64
00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:39.710
of the sanctifying presence of the Creator. Right?

65
00:03:40.300 --> 00:03:44.100
Adam and Eve didn't have something added to them as

66
00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:46.400
much as they lost something.

67
00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:51.080
They were holy by the continual presence and connection they had with God, but

68
00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:54.900
they lost that. They were created for God to be

69
00:03:54.980 --> 00:03:58.850
turned toward him, and they lost that sanctifying presence, and

70
00:03:58.860 --> 00:04:02.780
their nature bent in upon itself. It was designed to focus

71
00:04:02.820 --> 00:04:06.700
on God and his glory, and it twisted inward to focus on

72
00:04:06.740 --> 00:04:09.460
their own glory, their own way, their own self.

73
00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:13.840
And this emptiness, this twisting, this bending towards

74
00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:17.740
self is the essence of what sin is. Not

75
00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:21.510
just actions, but nature. A bend toward self and

76
00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:24.900
self-sovereignty. You say, "Darryl, are you just making this up?

77
00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:27.900
Have other people noticed this too?"

78
00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:32.530
Let me read you some lyrics from another popular song in the

79
00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:36.490
world. Okay? John Mayer wrote a song called "Gravity." He said, "Gravity is working

80
00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:39.430
against me. Gravity wants to bring me down.

81
00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:43.920
I'll never know what makes this man, with all the love

82
00:04:43.960 --> 00:04:47.380
that his heart can stand, dream of ways to throw it all

83
00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:51.080
away. Gravity is working against me.

84
00:04:51.480 --> 00:04:55.320
Gravity wants to bring me down. Twice as much ain't twice

85
00:04:55.360 --> 00:04:59.080
as good, and can't sustain like one half could.

86
00:05:00.080 --> 00:05:02.820
It's wanting more, it's going to bring me to my knees."

87
00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:04.480
Wow.

88
00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:08.500
There's a guy who knows.

89
00:05:09.560 --> 00:05:11.180
There's a guy who's fought it. He's struggled with it.

90
00:05:11.220 --> 00:05:14.060
He calls it gravity, but you know what it is that's pulling him down?

91
00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:18.400
It's the sin nature. He's twisted in upon himself, and he can't figure out

92
00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:18.720
why.

93
00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:23.160
Isaiah said, "We have turned everyone into his own way."

94
00:05:23.730 --> 00:05:24.520
That's gravity.

95
00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:29.620
Now, don't miss this. The world would look at that and say, "Well, that's not

96
00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:32.640
a bad thing. Go your way. Do your own thing.

97
00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:34.920
The highest thing is to thine own self be true."

98
00:05:36.580 --> 00:05:38.800
But this is the corruption that we have.

99
00:05:38.860 --> 00:05:40.330
And Christians realize

100
00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:45.120
that self-sovereignty is ultimately the cause

101
00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:46.640
of everything that's wrong with us.

102
00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:49.700
The heart of our problem is the problem of our heart.

103
00:05:52.520 --> 00:05:55.380
So it's ridiculously good at disguising itself.

104
00:05:56.160 --> 00:05:59.200
It can disguise itself as self-esteem.

105
00:05:59.220 --> 00:06:01.130
It can disguise itself as self-protection.

106
00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:02.740
In a million other forms

107
00:06:03.584 --> 00:06:07.484
But in the final analysis, it's a corrupting influence that exists

108
00:06:07.544 --> 00:06:11.484
behind things. It's a mixture of self in all things.

109
00:06:11.804 --> 00:06:15.164
Self-rights, focusing on and fighting for my own rights.

110
00:06:15.924 --> 00:06:17.394
Self-admiration,

111
00:06:18.364 --> 00:06:21.554
thinking of myself more highly than I think of others.

112
00:06:22.524 --> 00:06:26.324
How about self-interest? Taking greater interest in my own

113
00:06:26.384 --> 00:06:28.024
things than the things of others.

114
00:06:29.064 --> 00:06:32.824
How about self-pity? Feeling sorry for myself when things don't

115
00:06:32.884 --> 00:06:34.304
go my way.

116
00:06:35.324 --> 00:06:36.394
Self-righteousness,

117
00:06:37.464 --> 00:06:41.394
feeling that I am better, I am more right, and

118
00:06:41.424 --> 00:06:44.474
better morally than others. Self-indulgence,

119
00:06:45.404 --> 00:06:48.804
giving to myself privileges and perks that I might

120
00:06:48.864 --> 00:06:50.024
deny to others.

121
00:06:50.884 --> 00:06:54.844
Self-preservation, protecting myself and my wants

122
00:06:54.884 --> 00:06:58.384
and my needs at the cost of God's will or at the cost of others.

123
00:06:59.304 --> 00:07:02.104
Self-sufficiency, believing, sometimes

124
00:07:02.164 --> 00:07:05.444
subconsciously, that I can accomplish what is needed

125
00:07:05.604 --> 00:07:06.924
regardless of God's help.

126
00:07:07.904 --> 00:07:09.254
And how about self-will?

127
00:07:10.124 --> 00:07:12.674
Wanting and choosing my own way,

128
00:07:13.604 --> 00:07:16.544
rationalizing and excusing however I need to.

129
00:07:18.254 --> 00:07:20.924
These things are quite at home in churches, aren't they?

130
00:07:21.944 --> 00:07:25.904
A.W. Tozer, a writer, a brilliant quote, he said, "These may show themselves

131
00:07:25.924 --> 00:07:29.904
in the grosser forms such as self-promotion or egotism, but

132
00:07:29.964 --> 00:07:33.384
they are the underlying cause. They seem to almost

133
00:07:33.704 --> 00:07:37.534
feed off orthodoxy of beliefs, and are as at home at

134
00:07:37.534 --> 00:07:41.464
a Bible conference as they are in a tavern." Haven't you ever seen these Christians

135
00:07:41.504 --> 00:07:42.984
that are right in all the

136
00:07:43.864 --> 00:07:46.164
different ways, but it's like they're mad about it?

137
00:07:46.784 --> 00:07:49.924
And they're still selfish, and they're still angry, and they're still hurtful to

138
00:07:49.964 --> 00:07:50.704
other people.

139
00:07:51.824 --> 00:07:53.074
A.W. Tozer said, "Remember,

140
00:07:54.704 --> 00:07:57.744
Peter, who followed him, also rebuked him."

141
00:08:00.064 --> 00:08:01.824
Right? Now, I think most of you

142
00:08:02.804 --> 00:08:06.284
may have some pullback in you from calling these things

143
00:08:06.504 --> 00:08:08.764
evidences of the sinful nature. And here's why.

144
00:08:09.304 --> 00:08:13.184
Because the culture around us continually preaches to us that

145
00:08:13.204 --> 00:08:16.564
they are good. Like protect yourself. Look out for number one.

146
00:08:16.624 --> 00:08:19.064
Nobody else is going to do it. You're a snowflake. There's nobody else like you.

147
00:08:19.444 --> 00:08:21.844
But here's my question. Do these things sound like Jesus?

148
00:08:22.284 --> 00:08:22.784
Self-rights,

149
00:08:23.704 --> 00:08:24.154
self-pity,

150
00:08:25.124 --> 00:08:28.904
self-indulgence, self-preservation, self-sufficiency,

151
00:08:29.764 --> 00:08:30.344
self-will?

152
00:08:32.225 --> 00:08:32.365
No.

153
00:08:33.584 --> 00:08:34.024
They don't.

154
00:08:35.044 --> 00:08:39.024
And let me remind you, I don't care what the culture says, or

155
00:08:39.105 --> 00:08:43.044
what your church teaches, or what your college professor says, or what your

156
00:08:43.204 --> 00:08:46.744
brother-in-law once told you. I don't care.

157
00:08:47.404 --> 00:08:50.304
I only want one thing for you in this 40 days.

158
00:08:50.404 --> 00:08:54.364
I want as much of Jesus in you as God can get into you.

159
00:08:55.444 --> 00:08:59.304
That's what I want for me. We're not after common or ordinary.

160
00:08:59.314 --> 00:09:01.344
I don't want normal Christian life.

161
00:09:01.404 --> 00:09:04.144
I want maximum Jesus, maximum holiness.

162
00:09:05.844 --> 00:09:07.544
If you were to suck all the air out of this,

163
00:09:08.464 --> 00:09:11.284
put that cap back on, and then roll it in the mud.

164
00:09:12.504 --> 00:09:16.224
You'd have the emptiness of the lack on the inside, the

165
00:09:16.233 --> 00:09:19.624
deprivation that Adam and Eve suffered, the loss of the

166
00:09:19.704 --> 00:09:22.733
sanctifying presence of God that held them in shape.

167
00:09:23.564 --> 00:09:25.624
That's where we are. That's the cowboy in me.

168
00:09:26.554 --> 00:09:30.384
And the gravity that's pulling us down, like John Mayer talked about, that's the

169
00:09:30.444 --> 00:09:34.244
sinful nature. Because when God's gone, it's a vacuum that twists us up,

170
00:09:34.384 --> 00:09:38.024
literally bends us towards sin. John Wesley called

171
00:09:38.064 --> 00:09:40.024
it our bent to sinning.

172
00:09:40.884 --> 00:09:41.594
Richard Taylor,

173
00:09:42.673 --> 00:09:46.624
the Nazarene writer said, and I'm paraphrasing here, he said, "The sin nature is

174
00:09:46.664 --> 00:09:50.594
the leftover tendency to assume I'm in charge in

175
00:09:50.624 --> 00:09:53.184
the everyday non-sinful decisions of life."

176
00:09:54.944 --> 00:09:58.024
We're not just dirty, we also don't sit straight.

177
00:10:00.874 --> 00:10:03.764
The songwriter said, "Prone to wander, Lord, I feel it.

178
00:10:04.024 --> 00:10:07.944
Prone to leave the God I love." So what is God going to do about

179
00:10:08.024 --> 00:10:11.284
all this? Can he even fix it? Can he restore this?

180
00:10:11.364 --> 00:10:13.644
Can he clean up the outside and wash it off?

181
00:10:13.984 --> 00:10:17.684
Can he fill the inside and straighten out what has been

182
00:10:17.824 --> 00:10:18.144
bent?

183
00:10:19.324 --> 00:10:23.104
Yes, he can. That's what we're going to start talking about next.

184
00:10:23.264 --> 00:10:27.244
Now, thankfully, I have to tell you, this is about as dark as it gets. Okay?

185
00:10:27.324 --> 00:10:31.244
I know this is a heavy topic. If you can push through this far and

186
00:10:31.464 --> 00:10:35.324
bear to look into this mirror of the word of God and say, "Sinful

187
00:10:35.334 --> 00:10:38.744
nature is difficult, and hard, and sneaky, and selfish."

188
00:10:39.904 --> 00:10:42.554
If you can bear that, it's going to get brighter from here. All right?

189
00:10:42.564 --> 00:10:46.284
We're going to talk about how God sanctifies even the deepest parts of our

190
00:10:46.384 --> 00:10:50.184
sinful nature. Stick with me, because we're going to talk about how God

191
00:10:50.264 --> 00:10:53.864
refills, and straightens out, and washes off all that has been

192
00:10:53.984 --> 00:10:57.164
bent in our nature, all that has been bent within us.

193
00:10:57.264 --> 00:11:01.104
He fixes that which sin has broken. All right?

194
00:11:01.504 --> 00:11:03.964
So be encouraged.

195
00:11:04.904 --> 00:11:08.704
Good days are ahead. Lots of joy ahead as we talk about what

196
00:11:08.764 --> 00:11:12.744
God does to fix and repair that which is sinful.

197
00:11:13.584 --> 00:11:15.224
God bless you. We'll see you tomorrow.
